Subject: [PATCH] Configure production deployment: Vercel (frontend) + Render
 (backend)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- vite.config.ts: point Nitro at the "vercel" preset and emit straight into
  the Build Output API v3 layout (.vercel/output), since the default
  wrapper config only targets Cloudflare and skips Nitro entirely outside
  Lovable's sandbox — a plain `vite build` on Vercel's build machines was
  previously producing no deployable output at all.
- vercel.json: drive the build with bun and disable zero-config framework
  detection so Vercel doesn't treat this as a static Vite site; drop the
  old SPA rewrite-everything-to-/ rule, which conflicted with the SSR
  function + static screens now produced by the build.
- render.yaml: new Render Blueprint for the FastAPI backend (build/start
  commands, generated JWT secret, CORS/frontend URL env vars, notes on
  enabling a persistent disk for SQLite).
- backend/main.py: fix CORS_ORIGINS actually being applied — the env var
  was parsed but silently discarded, so every deployment fell back to the
  hardcoded localhost origin list and the browser blocked all API calls
  from a real frontend domain.
- backend/database.py: make the SQLite path configurable via DATABASE_URL
  for use with a persistent disk in production.
- public/screens/api.js: replace the hardcoded 127.0.0.1:8000 default with
  a hostname-aware default (local backend on localhost, deployed Render
  backend everywhere else), while keeping the window.__CASHPILOT_API_URL__
  override for edge cases.
- README: document the Vercel/Render deploy steps, required env vars, and
  known production limitations (ephemeral SQLite on Render's free plan,
  no transactional email for password reset, Render free-plan cold starts).

Verified locally: full production build (bun run build) generates a valid
.vercel/output Build Output API v3 payload — served it locally and
confirmed the SSR shell, static /screens/*.html pages, and JS assets all
resolve. Ran the FastAPI backend with production-style env vars
(CORS_ORIGINS/FRONTEND_URL/DATABASE_URL set, no GOOGLE_API_KEY) and
exercised all 22 endpoints (register/login/reset-password flow, dashboard,
invoice CRUD, analytics, payment priority/plan, scenario simulation, the
three AI endpoints correctly 503'ing without a Gemini key, CORS preflight
allow/deny, auth rejection) — all behaved correctly.

